       nneewwtteerrmm  are  called  (because  those  compute the screen size).  After
       uussee__ttiiooccttll is called with TTRRUUEE as an  argument,  _n_c_u_r_s_e_s  modifies  the
       last step in its computation of screen size as follows:

       •   checks  if the _L_I_N_E_S and _C_O_L_U_M_N_S environment variables are set to a
           number greater than zero.

       •   for each, _n_c_u_r_s_e_s updates the  corresponding  environment  variable
           with  the  value  that it has obtained via operating system call or
           from the terminal database.

       •   _n_c_u_r_s_e_s re-fetches the value of the environment variables  so  that
           it is still the environment variables which set the screen size.

